      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During the Revolutionary War, British General Charles Cornwallis retreated through Quinton toward Williamsburg in June 1781.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/quinton_virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Battle of Seven Pines began when Union General McClellan crossed the Chickahominy near Quinton, a pivotal Civil War clash.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/quinton_virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Watkins School, a National Historic Landmark, was central to the 1968 Supreme Court case Green v. County School Board of New Kent.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/quinton_virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Crump’s Mill and Millpond, historic watermill sites, sit on the National Register of Historic Places in Quinton.",
